<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h1 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto"><strong>References</strong></h1><a id="user-content-references" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: References" href="#references"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://docs.fedoraproject.org/en-US/packaging-guidelines/CryptoPolicies/" rel="nofollow">Fedora Packaging Policy for Crypto</a><br>
<a href="https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/SpecialPublications/NIST.SP.800-57pt1r5.pdf" rel="nofollow">NIST - Recommendation for Key Management</a> and especially section 5.6 Guidance for Cryptographic Algorithm and Key-Size Selection<br>
<a href="https://eprint.iacr.org/2013/635.pdf" rel="nofollow">Universal security from bits and mips to pools, lakes – and beyond</a> by Lenstra et al<br>
<a href="https://utcc.utoronto.ca/~cks/space/blog/spam/TLSExternalTypes-2023-04" rel="nofollow">TLS versions and ciphers used for inbound SMTP connections at Toronto University</a></p>
